# Copy this file to .env.local for local development (.env.local is git-ignored) and set the same two variables in
# your Vercel project (Settings -> Environment Variables), then redeploy: Vite reads them at BUILD time.
# Placeholders only. Never commit real values.

# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> "anon" / "publishable" key (safe for the browser).
# NEVER use the service_role / secret key here: anything starting with VITE_ is shipped to every visitor.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. Only set this if email links (confirm signup, reset password) must return somewhere other than the site
# the user is on. By default they return to the current site's root, which is what you want on Vercel.
# VITE_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL=
